iod 1901–2018</div>", "+        </div>", "+        <div class="metric-card hero">", "+          <div class="metric-value">3.3–3.6 billion</div>", "+          <div class="metric-label">People living in contexts highly vulnerable to climate change — nearly half of humanity exposed to severe climate hazards with cascading and compounding risks</div>", "+        </div>", "+        <div class="metric-card hero">", "+          <div class="metric-value">43% by 2030</div>", "+          <div class="metric-label">Required reduction in global GHG emissions below 2019 levels to limit warming to 1.5°C with no or limited overshoot — the window for action is narrowing rapidly</div>", "+        </div>", "+        <div class="metric-card">", "+          <div class="metric-value">~500 GtCO₂</div>", "+          <div class="metric-label">Remaining carbon budget from start of 2020<br>For a 50% chance of limiting warming to 1.5°C</div>", "+        </div>", "+        <div class="metric-card">", "+          <div class="metric-value">~40% loss</div>", "+          <div class="metric-label">Arctic sea ice extent decline in September<br>Compared to 1979–2020 average</div>", "+        </div>", "       </div>", "-      <div class="metric-card">", "-        <div class="metric-icon">🏭</div>", "-        <div class="metric-value">~59 GtCO₂e</div>", "-        <div class="metric-label">Global GHG emissions in 2019<br>Fossil fuel &amp; land-use change dominant</div>", "-      </div>", "-      <div class="metric-card">", "-        <div class="metric-icon">🌊</div>", "-        <div class="metric-value">~0.20 m</div>", "-        <div class="metric-label">Global mean sea level rise<br>1901&ndash;2018</div>", "-      </div>", "-      <div class="metric-card featured">", "-        <div class="metric-icon">⚠️</div>", "-        <div class="metric-value urgent">3.3&ndash;3.6 billion</div>", "-        <div class="metric-label">People living in contexts highly vulnerable to climate change &mdash; nearly half of hu